   "evidence": "Diffractive/Basic.lean:95-99 are the only occurrences of `MX2` in the repo (grep `MX2` over `code/EpsilonEridani`); `Kinematics/Basic.lean:79 lemma W2_expand` is the precedent for the same `(a+b)\u00b2` shape; roadmap `Diffraction/README.md:279,285` lists `M_X\u00b2 = (q + \u0394)\u00b2` and `\u03b2 = Q\u00b2/(Q\u00b2 + M_X\u00b2 \u2212 t)` in the claimed \u00a70.1.",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/QFT/Scattering/DIS/Diffractive/Basic.lean",
   "fix": "Add the expansion for symmetric `g`: `MX2 g K = g K.q K.q + 2 * g K.q (K.p - K.pPrime) + g (K.p - K.pPrime) (K.p - K.pPrime)`, and the one-line consequence `beta g K = K.Q2 g / (K.Q2 g + MX2 g K - g (K.p - K.pPrime) (K.p - K.pPrime))` (denominators are equal identically, so no non-degeneracy hypothesis is needed). The earlier contest rested on the `ExclKinematics`/`DisKinematics` split, which this head removes \u2014 `MX2` and `beta` now sit on one record, and the author's own reply concedes the relation is statable here.",
   "issue": "`MX2` has only `MX2_def`; nothing in the file or repo connects it to `Q2`, `beta`, `xi` or `\u0394\u00b2`. The parallel definition `W2 = (p+q)\u00b2` in the parent file ships with `W2_expand`; `MX2 = (q+\u0394)\u00b2` ships with nothing, so `Q\u00b2 + M_X\u00b2 \u2212 \u0394\u00b2 = 2 \u0394\u00b7q` \u2014 the content that makes `M_X\u00b2` usable \u2014 is reachable only by unfolding.",
   "line": 95
  }
